  "setting": "炭火未熄的石砌鍛坊",
  "subtitle": "",
  "subtitle_en": "",
  "lead": "她帶來一點火，穿過石院與長長的水廊。雨停以後，炭暗了。她走進工坊，看金屬在火裡變紅，再把它交給水。",
  "lead_en": "She brings a little fire through the stone courtyard. After the rain, the charcoal darkens. In the workshop, metal turns red, then meets the water.",
  "statement_title": "",
  "statement": "她帶來一點火，穿過石院與長長的水廊。雨停以後，炭暗了。她走進工坊，看金屬在火裡變紅，再把它交給水。\n\n火把影子留在牆上，水把光送回高處。等候的時候，她不必一直伸手。\n\n天亮時，有人接過鉗子。\n她倒出一壺清水。\n兩人走出院子，火留在身後。",
  "statement_en": "She brings a little fire through the stone courtyard. After the rain, the charcoal darkens. In the workshop, metal turns red, then meets the water.\n\nFire leaves a shadow on the wall. Water returns the light. While she waits, her hands can rest.\n\nAt dawn, another pair of hands takes the tongs.\nShe pours clear water.\nThey leave the courtyard together. The fire stays behind.",
  "afterword": "天亮時，有人接過鉗子。\n她倒出一壺清水。\n兩人走出院子，火留在身後。",
  "afterword_en": "At dawn, another pair of hands takes the tongs.\nShe pours clear water.\nThey leave the courtyard together. The fire stays behind.",
  "series_statement": "《神話未完成》\n史旺姬走進流傳至今的神話，留下它最核心的問題，讓它面對今天的生活。神話一直被講述、被使用，所以還沒有完成。",
  "series_statement_en": "Myths in the Making\nSwanky Ji steps into myths that are still being told, keeps the question at their heart, and lets it meet the life we live now. A myth that is still told and still used is not yet finished.",
